        <dt>RDF Unique Identifier</dt>
        <dd><a href="https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000097785.html">
            http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000097785
        </a></dd>

        
                <span id="scopeNote">
                    <dt>Scope Note</dt><dd>The use of various imaging and image enhancement techniques in forensic investigative disciplines. It often includes <a href="/record/ui?ui=D005554" class="textLink_FORENSICMEDICINE">FORENSIC MEDICINE</a> platforms such as <a href="/record/ui?ui=D014965" class="textLink_X-RAYS">X-RAYS</a>; CT XRAY; and MRI.</dd>
                </span>
            
                <dt>Entry Term(s)</dt>
                <dd>
                    Forensic Radiology
                    
                </dd>
            <dt>NLM Classification #</dt>
            <dd>W 775</dd>
        
                <dt>See Also</dt>
                
                    <dd><a id="seeAlso_PostmortemImaging"
                           href="/record/ui?ui=D000097873"
                        >Postmortem Imaging</a></dd>
                
            <dt>Public MeSH Note</dt><dd>2024</dd>
        
            <dt>History Note</dt><dd>2024</dd>
        
        


        
